  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Multi-Stakeholder Alliance for the Industrial Cassava Value Chain in PDET Municipalities of Sucre</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project contributes to the economic, agro-industrial development and food sovereignty of cassava producers in Montes de Mar&#xED;a, through interventions that leverage private and public resources and boost local regional markets, with a cross-cutting gender approach. The project seeks to close socioeconomic gaps and consolidate peace in the target territories, by promoting environmental sustainability and social inclusion through a model of reconciliation. The following entities will participate in the project: Almidones de Sucre, three organizations of small producers, Mayor&#x2019;s Offices of Toluviejo, Chalan and San Antonio de Palmito, Territory Renewal Agency, Rural Development Agency, Colombian Agricultural Institute, Agrosavia, Regional Autonomous Corporation of Sucre, National Learning Service, GERMISEMILLAS, Campo Limpio, Lombriabonos La Granja, Bancolombia Foundation, and Banco Agrario. Each participating entity within its role will contribute to economic and agro-industrial development promoting food sovereignty and supporting organizational and business strengthening processes, based on a gender and social inclusion approach. The cultivation of industrial cassava has high importance in the region as well as in the PDET municipalities. Likewise, this cultivation is prioritized in the Action Plans for Regional Transformation a planning instrument conceived in the Peace Agreement.</narrative>
  </description>
